  "summary": "Four documents directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to agricultural yield estimation, and one additional document applies decentralised training to the same topic (included as the fifth-best match given the absence of a fifth gradient-boosted-trees/yield paper). [V0037] (El-Sayed et al., 2022) evaluates boosted decision-tree ensembles on the AgriSat-4 dataset, reporting AUROC of 0.75. [V0039] (Gupta et al., 2024) applies the same method to the CellLife dataset, achieving accuracy of 0.89. [V0038] (Fischer et al., 2023) uses boosted decision-tree ensembles on LedgerGuard, obtaining F1 of 0.82. [V0040] (Haddad et al., 2025) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles to ToxiBench for agricultural yield estimation, reporting MAE of 0.61. [V0034] (El-Sayed et al., 2022) addresses agricultural yield but uses decentralised training without pooled records on LedgerGuard (AUROC 0.71), making it the weakest match. Documents mentioning boosted trees only in prior-work sentences (e.g., [V0097], [V0019], [V0168], [V0123]) are excluded as non-applications.",
